LESSONS["2A"].title="Experiences: Present Perfect";
LESSONS["2A"].titleFa="تجربه‌ها: حال کامل";
LESSONS["2A"].pretest=[{"q": "Jill says she always wanted to be an actor, and still does now. Which verb form does she use?", "o": ["wanted (simple past)", "has wanted (present perfect)", "wants (simple present)", "was wanting (past continuous)"], "a": 1, "ex": ""}, {"q": "Sonia talks about not saving money last year, connected to now. Which tense fits best?", "o": ["Present perfect", "Simple past", "Simple present", "Future"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "Raquel says her brother surfed in Hawai'i, but the exact time isn't important. Which tense fits this idea?", "o": ["Simple past", "Present perfect", "Present continuous", "Past perfect"], "a": 1, "ex": ""}, {"q": "Hiro says he went to Europe many times in the past, with a clear finished time period. Which tense does he use?", "o": ["Present perfect", "Simple past", "Present perfect continuous", "Simple future"], "a": 1, "ex": ""}];
LESSONS["2A"].grammar={points:[{"label": "نقطه ۱", "title": "Present perfect for indefinite time before now", "html": "<h3>قاعده</h3>\n<p>از <b>حال کامل (present perfect)</b> برای اتفاقاتی استفاده می‌کنیم که در زمانی نامشخص قبل از الان افتاده‌اند — زمان دقیق مهم نیست.</p>\n<div class=\"ex\">I've been to Europe. · I haven't been to Paris.</div>\n<div class=\"ex\">You've done a lot of things. · You haven't gone sailing.</div>\n<div class=\"ex\">He's surfed in Hawai'i. · She hasn't tried surfing before.</div>"}, {"label": "نقطه ۲", "title": "Frequency expressions", "html": "<h3>قید‌های تکرار با حال کامل</h3>\n<p>حال کامل معمولاً با این قیدهای تکرار همراه می‌آید:</p>\n<div class=\"ex\">I've <span class=\"hl\">always</span> wanted to study acting.</div>\n<div class=\"ex\">We've gone sailing <span class=\"hl\">once / twice / many times</span>.</div>\n<div class=\"ex\">She's <span class=\"hl\">never</span> tried it before.</div>"}, {"label": "نقطه ۳", "title": "been vs. gone", "html": "<h3>been در برابر gone</h3>\n<p><b>been</b> در واقع شکل سوم فعل <b>be</b> است (be → was/were → been)، نه فعل go. اما در حال کامل، وقتی درباره‌ی سفر صحبت می‌کنیم، been to به معنای «رفتن و برگشتن» به کار می‌رود. <b>gone</b> شکل سوم واقعیِ فعل go است و یعنی شخص هنوز آنجاست و برنگشته.</p>\n<div class=\"ex\">I've <span class=\"hl\">been</span> to Paris. <span class=\"note\">(رفتم و برگشتم)</span></div>\n<div class=\"ex\">She's <span class=\"hl\">gone</span> to Paris. <span class=\"note\">(الان آنجاست)</span></div>"}, {"label": "نقطه ۴", "title": "Negative form & irregular verbs", "html": "<h3>منفی کردن حال کامل</h3>\n<p>برای منفی کردن، <b>not</b> را بعد از have/has می‌آوریم: <b>haven't / hasn't + شکل سوم فعل (past participle)</b>.</p>\n<div class=\"ex\">I <span class=\"hl\">haven't been</span> to Paris. · She <span class=\"hl\">hasn't tried</span> surfing.</div>\n<h3>فعل‌های باقاعده و بی‌قاعده</h3>\n<p>فعل‌های باقاعده در شکل سوم مثل گذشته‌ی ساده با <b>-ed</b> ساخته می‌شوند (travel → traveled → traveled). اما بسیاری از پرکاربردترین فعل‌های انگلیسی <b>بی‌قاعده</b> هستند و باید حفظ شوند.</p>\n<div class=\"irr-table\">\n<table>\n<tr><th>Base</th><th>Past</th><th>Past Participle</th></tr>\n<tr><td>be</td><td>was/were</td><td>been</td></tr>\n<tr><td>go</td><td>went</td><td>gone</td></tr>\n<tr><td>do</td><td>did</td><td>done</td></tr>\n<tr><td>see</td><td>saw</td><td>seen</td></tr>\n<tr><td>eat</td><td>ate</td><td>eaten</td></tr>\n<tr><td>take</td><td>took</td><td>taken</td></tr>\n<tr><td>have</td><td>had</td><td>had</td></tr>\n<tr><td>make</td><td>made</td><td>made</td></tr>\n<tr><td>get</td><td>got</td><td>gotten</td></tr>\n<tr><td>give</td><td>gave</td><td>given</td></tr>\n<tr><td>write</td><td>wrote</td><td>written</td></tr>\n<tr><td>break</td><td>broke</td><td>broken</td></tr>\n<tr><td>speak</td><td>spoke</td><td>spoken</td></tr>\n<tr><td>find</td><td>found</td><td>found</td></tr>\n<tr><td>win</td><td>won</td><td>won</td></tr>\n<tr><td>lose</td><td>lost</td><td>lost</td></tr>\n<tr><td>forget</td><td>forgot</td><td>forgotten</td></tr>\n<tr><td>steal</td><td>stole</td><td>stolen</td></tr>\n<tr><td>drive</td><td>drove</td><td>driven</td></tr>\n<tr><td>fall</td><td>fell</td><td>fallen</td></tr>\n<tr><td>meet</td><td>met</td><td>met</td></tr>\n</table>\n</div>\n<div class=\"note\">این فهرست را حفظ کنید — این‌ها پرکاربردترین فعل‌های بی‌قاعده در حال کامل هستند.</div>"}],bookExA:[{"q": "A: I've always _____ to try rock climbing.", "o": ["want", "wanted"], "a": 1, "ex": ""}, {"q": "B: Not me. I've _____ wanted to. I've always been afraid of heights.", "o": ["never", "ever"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "A: I _____ the Grand Canyon. I really want to go there.", "o": ["haven't seen", "didn't see"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "B: My friend _____ there. She had an amazing time.", "o": ["has been", "was"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "A: I've _____ surfing three or four times. It's exciting.", "o": ["gone", "went"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "B: I _____ it before. I've never done any water sports.", "o": ["haven't tried", "didn't try"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "A: My dream is to be a tennis player. I've _____ a lot of training.", "o": ["had", "have"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "B: No way! I've always _____ to meet Andy Murray.", "o": ["wanted", "want"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "A: We _____ much, but we want to go to Bogotá.", "o": ["haven't traveled", "didn't travel"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "B: He's _____ me several times, but I haven't saved enough money.", "o": ["invited", "invite"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}],extraQuiz1:[{"q": "I've _____ been to Japan.", "o": ["never", "yesterday"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "She's _____ wanted to learn the piano.", "o": ["always", "yesterday"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "Have you _____ tried sushi?", "o": ["ever", "yet ago"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "He's _____ to London — he's still there.", "o": ["gone", "been"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "I've _____ to London — I came back last week.", "o": ["been", "gone"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "We've traveled to Asia _____.", "o": ["many times", "yesterday"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "They _____ never gone camping.", "o": ["have", "did"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "She's _____ surfed before.", "o": ["never", "ago"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "I've done a lot of things, but I _____ gone sailing.", "o": ["haven't", "didn't"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "He's _____ been to Rome twice.", "o": ["already", "yesterday"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}],extraQuiz2:[{"q": "_____ you ever eaten sushi?", "o": ["Have", "Did"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "Yes, I _____. I ate it last week.", "o": ["have", "has"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "_____ you ever traveled alone?", "o": ["Have", "Was"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "I've _____ wanted to visit Egypt.", "o": ["always", "last year"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "She's traveled to Peru _____.", "o": ["once", "yesterday"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "We haven't seen that movie _____.", "o": ["yet", "ago"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "He's _____ climbed a mountain before.", "o": ["never", "already gone"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "I've _____ to Mexico. I loved it!", "o": ["been", "gone"], "a": 0, "ex": "been to = رفتن و برگشتن؛ اینجا گوینده الان آنجا نیست."}, {"q": "They've _____ to Brazil — they're still there now.", "o": ["gone", "been"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "She's _____ done anything like that.", "o": ["never", "yesterday"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}]};
LESSONS["2A"].convo1=[{"q": "What's something you've always wanted to try but never have?", "sample": "Hmm, let me think for a second... I've always wanted to try skydiving, actually — it's been on my list for years. I've never actually done it, though, mainly because I've always been a little afraid of heights, if I'm honest. My friend's done it twice now, and every time she talks about it she says it's absolutely amazing, like nothing else compares to that feeling. I've thought about signing up so many times, but I always end up chickening out at the last minute. Maybe I'll finally work up the courage and try it someday — I keep telling myself this is the year, ha.", "glossary": {}, "hl": ["always", "never", "done"]}];
LESSONS["2A"].convo2=[{"q": "Have you ever done something a little crazy or adventurous?", "sample": "Yeah, actually, I have — I've gone bungee jumping once, and honestly, it was terrifying! I remember standing at the edge and just thinking, why am I doing this to myself. I'd never done anything like that before in my life, so my legs were shaking the whole time. I've also gone white-water rafting a couple of times with friends, which was a lot of fun, but bungee jumping was definitely scarier by far. I haven't tried skydiving yet, though — that one still kind of terrifies me just thinking about it — but maybe one day I'll be brave enough to give it a shot too.", "glossary": {}, "hl": ["gone", "never", "before", "tried", "yet"]}];
LESSONS["2A"].sessions=[{"id": "cb1", "stage": "Coursebook", "icon": "💬", "title": "Four Experiences", "fa": "متن: چهار نفر، چهار تجربه", "parts": [{"t": "context", "label": "Context", "title": "How do they talk about their experiences?", "lines": [{"sp": "Jill", "text": "I always wanted to be an actor as a child. I want to be an actor now."}, {"sp": "Sonia", "text": "We didn't save enough money last year. We don't have enough money now."}, {"sp": "Raquel", "text": "My brother even surfed in Hawai'i — exactly when isn't important."}, {"sp": "Hiro", "text": "In the past, I went to Europe many times."}]}]}, {"id": "cb2", "stage": "Coursebook", "icon": "⭕", "title": "Pre-test", "fa": "پیش‌آزمون", "parts": [{"t": "selfcheck", "key": "pretest", "label": "Pre-test"}]}, {"id": "cb3", "stage": "Coursebook", "icon": "📝", "title": "Present Perfect", "fa": "آموزش: حال کامل", "parts": [{"t": "teach", "pts": [0, 1, 2, 3]}]}, {"id": "cb4", "stage": "Coursebook", "icon": "✅", "title": "Exercise", "fa": "تمرین A کتاب", "parts": [{"t": "bookExercise", "key": "bookExA", "label": "Exercise"}]}, {"id": "ex1", "stage": "Extra", "icon": "📚", "title": "Vocabulary 1", "fa": "لغات ۱", "parts": [{"t": "vocab", "from": 0, "to": 10}, {"t": "matching", "sets": [1, 2]}]}, {"id": "ex2", "stage": "Extra", "icon": "📚", "title": "Vocabulary 2", "fa": "لغات ۲", "parts": [{"t": "vocab", "from": 10, "to": 20}, {"t": "matching", "sets": [3, 4]}, {"t": "gap"}]}, {"id": "ex3", "stage": "Extra", "icon": "🎯", "title": "Grammar Quiz 1", "fa": "آزمون گرامر ۱", "parts": [{"t": "quizset", "key": "extraQuiz1", "label": "Grammar Quiz 1"}]}, {"id": "ex4", "stage": "Extra", "icon": "🎯", "title": "Grammar Quiz 2", "fa": "آزمون گرامر ۲", "parts": [{"t": "quizset", "key": "extraQuiz2", "label": "Grammar Quiz 2"}]}, {"id": "ex5", "stage": "Extra", "icon": "🗣️", "title": "Conversation Practice 1", "fa": "تمرین مکالمه ۱", "parts": [{"t": "convo", "key": "convo1"}]}, {"id": "ex6", "stage": "Extra", "icon": "🗣️", "title": "Conversation Practice 2", "fa": "تمرین مکالمه ۲", "parts": [{"t": "convo", "key": "convo2"}]}, {"id": "ex7", "stage": "Extra", "icon": "📖", "title": "Article 1", "fa": "مقاله ۱", "parts": [{"t": "reading", "text": 0}]}, {"id": "ex8", "stage": "Extra", "icon": "📖", "title": "Article 2", "fa": "مقاله ۲", "parts": [{"t": "reading", "text": 1}]}, {"id": "ex9", "stage": "Extra", "icon": "✍️", "title": "Writing", "fa": "نوشتن", "parts": [{"t": "writing"}]}];

/* ---- Unit 2 Lesson B: Present perfect vs simple past ---- */
LESSONS["2B"].pretest=[{"q": "Unscramble: to Ecuador / you / been / Have / ever", "o": ["Have you ever been to Ecuador?", "You have ever been to Ecuador?", "Ever have you been to Ecuador?", "Have ever you been to Ecuador?"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "B: Yes, I _____. I went there last year.", "o": ["have", "went"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "Unscramble: entered / you / Have / a talent contest / ever", "o": ["Have you ever entered a talent contest?", "You have ever entered a talent contest?", "Ever you have entered a talent contest?", "Have entered you ever a talent contest?"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "B: No, I _____. But I sang in a concert in May.", "o": ["haven't", "didn't"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}];
LESSONS["2B"].grammar={points:[{"label": "نقطه ۱", "title": "Present perfect for indefinite times before now", "html": "<h3>قاعده</h3>\n<p>از <b>حال کامل</b> برای پرسیدن یا صحبت درباره‌ی تجربه‌ها در زمانی نامشخص قبل از الان استفاده می‌کنیم.</p>\n<div class=\"ex\">Have you ever gone white-water rafting?</div>\n<div class=\"ex\">No, I haven't. I've never gone rafting.</div>\n<div class=\"ex\">Yes, I have. I went rafting last May.</div>"}, {"label": "نقطه ۲", "title": "Simple past for specific times", "html": "<h3>قاعده</h3>\n<p>وقتی زمان دقیق مشخص است (یا درباره‌ی جزئیات آن اتفاق خاص صحبت می‌کنیم)، از <b>گذشته‌ی ساده</b> استفاده می‌کنیم.</p>\n<div class=\"ex\">Did you have a good time?</div>\n<div class=\"ex\">Yes, I did. But I fell off the raft.</div>\n<div class=\"note\">معمولاً اول با حال کامل می‌پرسیم «آیا تا حالا...؟» و بعد با گذشته‌ی ساده جزئیات آن را می‌گوییم.</div>"}, {"label": "نقطه ۳", "title": "Past participles for experiences", "html": "<h3>شکل سوم فعل (Past Participle) برای «تا حالا...؟»</h3>\n<p>برای سؤالات Have you ever...؟ به شکل سوم فعل نیاز داریم. بسیاری از این فعل‌ها بی‌قاعده هستند:</p>\n<div class=\"irr-table\"><table>\n<tr><th>Base</th><th>Simple Past</th><th>Past Participle</th></tr>\n<tr><td>win</td><td>won</td><td>won</td></tr>\n<tr><td>find</td><td>found</td><td>found</td></tr>\n<tr><td>fall</td><td>fell</td><td>fallen</td></tr>\n<tr><td>get</td><td>got</td><td>gotten</td></tr>\n<tr><td>take</td><td>took</td><td>taken</td></tr>\n<tr><td>lose</td><td>lost</td><td>lost</td></tr>\n<tr><td>forget</td><td>forgot</td><td>forgotten</td></tr>\n<tr><td>hurt</td><td>hurt</td><td>hurt</td></tr>\n<tr><td>speak</td><td>spoke</td><td>spoken</td></tr>\n<tr><td>have</td><td>had</td><td>had</td></tr>\n<tr><td>break</td><td>broke</td><td>broken</td></tr>\n<tr><td>steal</td><td>stole</td><td>stolen</td></tr>\n</table></div>\n<div class=\"ex\">Have you ever <span class=\"hl\">won</span> a prize? · Have you ever <span class=\"hl\">broken</span> something valuable?</div>"}],bookExA:[{"q": "A: _____ you ever _____ of kitesurfing?", "o": ["Have / heard", "Did / hear"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "B: Yes, I have. But I've _____ done anything like that.", "o": ["never", "ever"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "A: _____ you and your friends ever _____ on a big roller coaster?", "o": ["Have / gone", "Did / go"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "B: No, we haven't. I've always _____ roller coasters.", "o": ["hated", "hate"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "A: _____ you ever _____ up all night?", "o": ["Have / stayed", "Did / stay"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "B: Yes, I have. My family _____ camping two years ago.", "o": ["went", "have gone"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "...and none of us _____ all night.", "o": ["slept", "have slept"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "A: _____ you _____ anything different last summer?", "o": ["Did / do", "Have / done"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "B: Yes, I did. I _____ to play African drums.", "o": ["learned", "have learned"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "I've always _____ to play them, but I've never _____ to Africa.", "o": ["wanted / gone", "want / go"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}],buildingVocab:[{"q": "Have you ever _____ (win) a prize?", "o": ["won", "winned"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "Have you ever _____ (break) something valuable?", "o": ["broken", "breaked"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "Have you ever _____ (get) 100% on a test?", "o": ["gotten", "getted"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "Have you ever _____ (lose) something important?", "o": ["lost", "losed"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "Have you ever _____ (speak) to a famous person?", "o": ["spoken", "speaked"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "Have you ever _____ (have) the flu?", "o": ["had", "haved"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "Have you ever _____ (take) an exciting trip?", "o": ["taken", "taked"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "Have you ever _____ (forget) someone's birthday?", "o": ["forgotten", "forgetted"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "Have you ever _____ (find) a wallet?", "o": ["found", "finded"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "Have you ever _____ (fall) and hurt yourself?", "o": ["fallen", "falled"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "Has anyone ever _____ (steal) something from you?", "o": ["stolen", "stealed"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "Have you ever _____ (hurt) yourself badly?", "o": ["hurt", "hurted"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}],extraQuiz1:[{"q": "Have you ever _____ scuba diving?", "o": ["gone", "went"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "Yes, I _____. I went last summer.", "o": ["have", "did"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "_____ you go with a friend?", "o": ["Did", "Have"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "Yes, I _____. We had a great time.", "o": ["did", "have"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "She's _____ won a prize before.", "o": ["never", "yesterday"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "_____ you ever broken something valuable?", "o": ["Have", "Did"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "I broke my phone _____.", "o": ["last week", "ever"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "Have you ever _____ 100% on a test?", "o": ["gotten", "got yesterday"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "She's _____ lost her keys twice this month.", "o": ["already", "yesterday"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "_____ you found a wallet before?", "o": ["Have", "Did"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}],extraQuiz2:[{"q": "Has he ever _____ the flu?", "o": ["had", "has"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "Yes, he _____. He was sick last winter.", "o": ["was", "has"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "_____ you ever forgotten someone's birthday?", "o": ["Have", "Did"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "Yes, I _____. It was my sister's birthday last year.", "o": ["did", "have"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "_____ you fallen and hurt yourself recently?", "o": ["Have", "Did"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "No, I _____. But I fell last winter.", "o": ["haven't", "didn't"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "She's _____ spoken to a famous person.", "o": ["never", "last year"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "_____ you take an exciting trip last year?", "o": ["Did", "Have"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "Yes, I _____. I went to Peru.", "o": ["did", "have"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "Have you ever _____ something important?", "o": ["lost", "lose yesterday"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}]};
LESSONS["2B"].convo1=[{"q": "Have you ever done something that scared you a lot?", "sample": "Yeah, actually, I have — I went white-water rafting once with a group of friends, and at one point I actually fell out of the raft! I've genuinely never been so scared in my life, the current was so strong. Luckily my friends pulled me back in pretty fast, but for those few seconds my heart was absolutely racing and I couldn't even think straight. Afterward everyone was laughing about it, but honestly it took me a while to see the funny side. I haven't been rafting since, but I don't regret trying it — have you ever done anything like that?", "glossary": {}, "hl": ["went", "fell", "never", "been"]}];
LESSONS["2B"].convo2=[{"q": "Have you ever performed in front of a lot of people?", "sample": "Yes, actually, I have! I entered a talent contest a couple of years ago and sang in front of what felt like a huge crowd — probably around a hundred people, if not more. It was really scary, honestly, my hands were shaking the entire time I was walking up to the microphone. But somehow I got through it, and I ended up winning third place, so in the end it was totally worth all that nervousness. I haven't done anything like that since, though — I think one performance like that is enough for a lifetime! Maybe someday I'll work up the courage to try again.", "glossary": {}, "hl": ["entered", "sang", "haven't", "since"]}];
LESSONS["2B"].sessions=[{"id": "cb1", "stage": "Coursebook", "icon": "💬", "title": "Have You Ever...?", "fa": "متن: کار ترسناکی انجام داده‌اید؟", "parts": [{"t": "context", "label": "Context", "title": "Have You Ever Done Anything Scary?", "lines": [{"sp": "Mei-ling Chen (Taipei, Taiwan)", "text": "Yes, I have. I went white-water rafting in Ecuador last year, and I fell off the raft. Luckily, my friends pulled me out of the river. But I've never been so scared in my life."}, {"sp": "Martín Suárez (Caracas, Venezuela)", "text": "No, I haven't. Well, maybe once. I entered a talent contest a couple of years ago and sang in front of a hundred people. That was scary. But I won third place!"}]}]}, {"id": "cb2", "stage": "Coursebook", "icon": "⭕", "title": "Pre-test", "fa": "پیش‌آزمون", "parts": [{"t": "selfcheck", "key": "pretest", "label": "Pre-test"}]}, {"id": "cb3", "stage": "Coursebook", "icon": "📝", "title": "Present Perfect vs. Past", "fa": "آموزش: حال کامل و گذشته‌ی ساده", "parts": [{"t": "teach", "pts": [0, 1]}]}, {"id": "cb4", "stage": "Coursebook", "icon": "✅", "title": "Exercise", "fa": "تمرین A کتاب", "parts": [{"t": "bookExercise", "key": "bookExA", "label": "Exercise"}]}, {"id": "cb5", "stage": "Coursebook", "icon": "🔁", "title": "Past Participles", "fa": "تقویت واژگان", "parts": [{"t": "teach", "pts": [2], "label": "Grammar"}, {"t": "bookExercise", "key": "buildingVocab", "label": "Exercise"}]}, {"id": "ex1", "stage": "Extra", "icon": "📚", "title": "Vocabulary 1", "fa": "لغات ۱", "parts": [{"t": "vocab", "from": 0, "to": 10}, {"t": "matching", "sets": [1, 2]}]}, {"id": "ex2", "stage": "Extra", "icon": "📚", "title": "Vocabulary 2", "fa": "لغات ۲", "parts": [{"t": "vocab", "from": 10, "to": 20}, {"t": "matching", "sets": [3, 4]}, {"t": "gap"}]}, {"id": "ex3", "stage": "Extra", "icon": "🎯", "title": "Grammar Quiz 1", "fa": "آزمون گرامر ۱", "parts": [{"t": "quizset", "key": "extraQuiz1", "label": "Grammar Quiz 1"}]}, {"id": "ex4", "stage": "Extra", "icon": "🎯", "title": "Grammar Quiz 2", "fa": "آزمون گرامر ۲", "parts": [{"t": "quizset", "key": "extraQuiz2", "label": "Grammar Quiz 2"}]}, {"id": "ex5", "stage": "Extra", "icon": "🗣️", "title": "Conversation Practice 1", "fa": "تمرین مکالمه ۱", "parts": [{"t": "convo", "key": "convo1"}]}, {"id": "ex6", "stage": "Extra", "icon": "🗣️", "title": "Conversation Practice 2", "fa": "تمرین مکالمه ۲", "parts": [{"t": "convo", "key": "convo2"}]}, {"id": "ex7", "stage": "Extra", "icon": "📖", "title": "Article 1", "fa": "مقاله ۱", "parts": [{"t": "reading", "text": 0}]}, {"id": "ex8", "stage": "Extra", "icon": "📖", "title": "Article 2", "fa": "مقاله ۲", "parts": [{"t": "reading", "text": 1}]}, {"id": "ex9", "stage": "Extra", "icon": "✍️", "title": "Writing", "fa": "نوشتن", "parts": [{"t": "writing"}]}];

/* ---- Unit 2 Lesson C: conversation strategies ---- */
LESSONS["2C"].grammar={points:[{"label": "استراتژی ۱", "title": "Showing interest and asking a follow-up question", "html": "<h3>قاعده</h3>\n<p>برای زنده نگه‌داشتن مکالمه، ابتدا با جمله‌ای کوتاه علاقه نشان می‌دهیم (مثل <b>I've heard good things about it</b>)، سپس بلافاصله یک سؤال می‌پرسیم.</p>\n<div class=\"ex\">\"Have you been there?\" → \"No, but <span class=\"hl\">I've heard good things about it</span>. How was it?\"</div>\n<div class=\"note\">این کار مکالمه را طبیعی و دوطرفه نگه می‌دارد، به‌جای اینکه فقط با «بله/نه» جواب بدهیم.</div>"},{"label": "استراتژی ۲", "title": "Response questions — Do you? Have you?", "html": "<h3>قاعده</h3>\n<p>می‌توانید با یک سؤال کوتاه مثل <b>Do you?</b> یا <b>Have you?</b> علاقه نشان دهید. زمان فعل باید با جمله‌ی طرف مقابل یکی باشد.</p>\n<div class=\"ex\">\"I've seen it a couple of times.\" → \"<span class=\"hl\">Have you?</span>\"</div>\n<div class=\"note\">برای نشان دادن تعجب، از حالت غیررسمی‌تر مثل <b>You do?</b> یا <b>You have?</b> استفاده می‌شود.</div>"}],bookExC4:[{"q": "I just saw Hereafter. It was a good movie. Have you ever seen it?", "o": ["No, but I've heard good things about it. What's it about?", "It's a fruit, right? I've never tried one.", "No, but I've walked by it. What kind of food do they serve?", "No, but I've heard of it. What's it about?"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "Have you ever eaten a lychee?", "o": ["It's a fruit, right? I've never tried one. What do they taste like?", "No, but I've heard good things about them. What kind of music do they play?", "No, but I've walked by it. What kind of food do they serve?", "No, but I've heard of it. What's it about?"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "I heard a really good band called Sunset recently. Do you know them?", "o": ["No, but I've heard good things about them. What kind of music do they play?", "It's a fruit, right? I've never tried one.", "No, but I've walked by it. What kind of food do they serve?", "No, but I've heard of it. What's it about?"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "One of my favorite restaurants is Spice House. Have you ever eaten there?", "o": ["No, but I've walked by it. What kind of food do they serve?", "It's a fruit, right? I've never tried one.", "No, but I've heard good things about them. What kind of music do they play?", "No, but I've heard of it. What's it about?"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}],bookExC6:[{"q": "A: I've never been up in a hot air balloon. I'm afraid of heights. B: ___? Me too, I hate flying. A: ___? I get sick on airplanes too. — What does B say first?", "o": ["Are you?", "Have you?", "Do you?", "Did you?"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "...and what does A say next?", "o": ["Are you?", "Have you?", "Do you?", "Did you?"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "A: Have you ever performed in front of an audience? B: Yes, I have. I do it all the time. A: ___? — Wow.", "o": ["Do you?", "Have you?", "Are you?", "Did you?"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "B: Yeah, I'm a drummer in a rock band. A: ___! — I'm impressed.", "o": ["Are you?", "Do you?", "Have you?", "Did you?"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "A: Have you seen any good movies lately? B: I went to see that new action movie that's out now. A: ___? The one with Liam Neeson?", "o": ["Did you?", "Have you?", "Are you?", "Do you?"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "B: I've seen all his movies. A: ___? So is he your favorite actor?", "o": ["Have you?", "Did you?", "Are you?", "Do you?"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}]};
LESSONS["2C"].sessions=[{"id": "cs1", "stage": "Coursebook", "icon": "💬", "title": "Conversation", "fa": "متن کامل مکالمه", "parts": [{"t": "context", "label": "Context", "title": "Lea and Jason talk about their week", "lines": [{"sp": "Lea", "text": "Have you done anything fun lately?"}, {"sp": "Jason", "text": "Yeah, we went to a new club called Fizz last week. Have you been there?"}, {"sp": "Lea", "text": "No, but I've heard good things about it. How was it?"}, {"sp": "Jason", "text": "Yeah, it's neat. The DJ was really good. Do you like techno music?"}, {"sp": "Lea", "text": "Yeah, it's OK, um, not my favorite. I prefer hip-hop."}, {"sp": "Jason", "text": "Do you? Have you seen that new movie about hip-hop artists?"}, {"sp": "Lea", "text": "No. Is it good?"}, {"sp": "Jason", "text": "Yeah. I've seen it a couple of times."}, {"sp": "Lea", "text": "Have you? Well, I'm kind of in the mood for a movie. Do you want to see it again?"}, {"sp": "Jason", "text": "Well, I enjoyed it, but... I've never seen a movie three times!"}]}]}, {"id": "cs2", "stage": "Coursebook", "icon": "📝", "title": "Showing Interest", "fa": "توضیح: نشان دادن علاقه", "parts": [{"t": "teach", "pts": [0]}]}, {"id": "cs3", "stage": "Coursebook", "icon": "👆", "title": "Find the pattern", "fa": "الگو را پیدا کنید", "parts": [{"t": "tapfind", "prompt": "Tap every line where Lea or Jason show interest and then ask a follow-up question.", "lines": [{"sp": "Lea", "text": "Have you done anything fun lately?"}, {"sp": "Jason", "text": "Yeah, we went to a new club called Fizz last week. Have you been there?"}, {"sp": "Lea", "text": "No, but I've heard good things about it. How was it?"}, {"sp": "Jason", "text": "Yeah, it's neat. The DJ was really good. Do you like techno music?"}, {"sp": "Lea", "text": "Yeah, it's OK, um, not my favorite. I prefer hip-hop."}, {"sp": "Jason", "text": "Do you? Have you seen that new movie about hip-hop artists?"}, {"sp": "Lea", "text": "No. Is it good?"}, {"sp": "Jason", "text": "Yeah. I've seen it a couple of times."}, {"sp": "Lea", "text": "Have you? Well, I'm kind of in the mood for a movie. Do you want to see it again?"}, {"sp": "Jason", "text": "Well, I enjoyed it, but... I've never seen a movie three times!"}]}]}, {"id": "cs4", "stage": "Coursebook", "icon": "✅", "title": "Exercise", "fa": "تمرین D کتاب", "parts": [{"t": "bookExercise", "key": "bookExC4", "label": "Exercise"}]}, {"id": "cs5", "stage": "Coursebook", "icon": "➕", "title": "Response Questions", "fa": "توضیح: سؤال‌های پاسخی", "parts": [{"t": "teach", "pts": [1]}]}, {"id": "cs6", "stage": "Coursebook", "icon": "✅", "title": "More Practice", "fa": "تمرین سؤال‌های پاسخی", "parts": [{"t": "bookExercise", "key": "bookExC6", "label": "Exercise"}]}, {"id": "ex1", "stage": "Extra", "icon": "📚", "title": "Vocabulary 1", "fa": "لغات ۱", "parts": [{"t": "vocab", "from": 0, "to": 10}, {"t": "matching", "sets": [1, 2]}]}, {"id": "ex2", "stage": "Extra", "icon": "📚", "title": "Vocabulary 2", "fa": "لغات ۲", "parts": [{"t": "vocab", "from": 10, "to": 20}, {"t": "matching", "sets": [3, 4]}, {"t": "gap"}]}, {"id": "ex3", "stage": "Extra", "icon": "📖", "title": "Article 1", "fa": "مقاله ۱", "parts": [{"t": "reading", "text": 0}]}, {"id": "ex4", "stage": "Extra", "icon": "📖", "title": "Article 2", "fa": "مقاله ۲", "parts": [{"t": "reading", "text": 1}]}, {"id": "ex5", "stage": "Extra", "icon": "✍️", "title": "Writing", "fa": "نوشتن", "parts": [{"t": "writing"}]}];

/* ---- Unit 2 Lesson D: reading + writing ---- */
LESSONS["2D"].mainReading=[{"title": "Travel Blogs", "topic": "Jake in Guatemala, Chloe in Brazil", "text": "JAKE'S JOURNEY — MARCH 2, GUATEMALA\nWhen we arrived in Guatemala two weeks ago, we didn't know what to expect. But I have to say, we've had a great time. I've done a lot of traveling, and I think it's one of the most amazing places I've ever been to. We've done a lot in the last two weeks. We've gone hiking, explored some of the ancient Mayan ruins, and camped next to a volcano. We've also seen some beautiful birds. The quetzals are so colorful, and there are hummingbirds everywhere. There are lots of things we haven't had time to do. I've always wanted to go to the rain forest. I hope we get there.\n\nCamping was really fun. We drove up some rough dirt roads to Ipala Volcano and got a flat tire on the way. It was worth the trip, though. There's a really pretty lake up there that we hiked around. It rained really hard one night, and everything outside the tent got soaked, but at least the tent didn't leak. Fortunately, the weather's gotten better. Another place we found had these beautiful hot springs and a hot waterfall. Standing underneath it was just like taking a hot shower! I miss you all!\n\nComments — Linh: You do? That's hard to believe, Jake. It sounds like you're having a blast! I've never been to Central America, but I've always wanted to go there. Have you gone on one of the zip lines? I've heard you can do them there. Have fun!\n\nCHLOE'S TRAVELS\nAfter 36 hours of travel, we arrived in Brazil last Sunday. I can't believe it — we got stuck on our way here, and unfortunately, we missed Carnival in Rio! I've always wanted to see it — with all the costumes and dancing and music, but we just couldn't get here in time. And I lost my camera!\n\nFortunately, I've been good about uploading all my photos to the blog, so I haven't lost many. At least it wasn't an expensive camera. Anyway, we've been to the beach every day. We've gone surfing, and I went parasailing yesterday. The views were amazing!\n\nWe've done a lot of sightseeing — though we haven't taken the cable car up Sugar Loaf Mountain. We'll probably do that tomorrow. We've met some really nice people. They're so incredibly friendly and helpful. Amazingly, we managed to visit the family of one of our classmates from college. They were extremely generous. They made us some traditional feijoada — a bean and meat dish. It was delicious! I could happily spend another month here. We'll have to come back and visit again.\n\nComments — Steve: Hey Chloe. I miss you! It's cold and wet here, and I'm working, unfortunately. Have you been able to see any capoeira?", "glossary": {}, "hl": ["fortunately", "unfortunately", "amazingly", "incredibly", "extremely"], "gist": {"q": "What are Jake and Chloe's blog posts mainly about?", "o": ["Two travelers sharing what they've experienced so far on their trips", "A guide to the best hotels in Central and South America", "A complaint about flight delays"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, "detailed": [{"q": "Is Guatemala exactly what Jake expected?", "o": ["No — he didn't know what to expect, but he's had a great time", "Yes, exactly as planned", "No, he hated it"], "a": 0, "ex": "او می‌گوید نمی‌دانستیم چه انتظاری داشته باشیم."}, {"q": "Has the weather been bad for Jake's entire trip?", "o": ["No — it rained hard one night, but the weather's gotten better", "Yes, it has rained every day", "No, it's been perfect the whole time"], "a": 0, "ex": "فقط یک شب باران شدید بود، بعد هوا بهتر شد."}, {"q": "Did Jake have a problem with his tent one night?", "o": ["No — the tent didn't leak, even though it rained hard", "Yes, the tent leaked badly", "Yes, the tent blew away"], "a": 0, "ex": "با اینکه باران شدید بود، چادر نم نداد."}, {"q": "Did Chloe enjoy Carnival?", "o": ["No — she and her friends missed it entirely", "Yes, it was her favorite part", "She only saw part of it"], "a": 0, "ex": "آن‌ها به موقع نرسیدند و کارناوال را از دست دادند."}, {"q": "Have Chloe and her friends finished all their sightseeing?", "o": ["No — they still haven't taken the cable car up Sugar Loaf Mountain", "Yes, they've seen everything", "They didn't do any sightseeing"], "a": 0, "ex": "هنوز سوار تله‌کابین نشده‌اند."}, {"q": "Would Chloe like to spend more time in Brazil?", "o": ["Yes — she says she could happily spend another month there", "No, she wants to go home", "She doesn't say"], "a": 0, "ex": "می‌گوید could happily spend another month here."}]}];
LESSONS["2D"].writingTask={"title": "A travel experience", "text": "Write a short blog post (100–150 words) about a trip or an experience you've had, using the present perfect to talk about what you've done, and at least two adverbs of attitude (fortunately, unfortunately, amazingly, luckily, surprisingly...)."};
LESSONS["2D"].grammar=undefined;
LESSONS["2D"].sessions=[{"id": "cb1", "stage": "Coursebook", "icon": "🔎", "title": "Scan first", "fa": "ابتدا مرور سریع کنید", "parts": [{"t": "scanpre", "src": "mainReading", "text": 0}]}, {"id": "cb2", "stage": "Coursebook", "icon": "📖", "title": "Reading", "fa": "متن کامل", "parts": [{"t": "fullread", "src": "mainReading", "text": 0}]}, {"id": "cb3", "stage": "Coursebook", "icon": "✅", "title": "Comprehension", "fa": "درک مطلب", "parts": [{"t": "comprehension", "src": "mainReading", "text": 0}]}, {"id": "cb4", "stage": "Coursebook", "icon": "📝", "title": "Sample", "fa": "نمونه‌ی نوشتاری", "parts": [{"t": "writingSample", "title": "Flying Above the Rain Forest", "text": "FLYING ABOVE THE RAIN FOREST\n\nLast summer, I went on the Sky Trek in the rain forest in Monteverde, Costa Rica. I'm afraid of heights, so I almost didn't go. Fortunately, there were some great guides, and they really helped me. Amazingly, it wasn't really scary. It was the most exciting experience I've ever had! I didn't see a quetzal bird, unfortunately, so I'll just have to go back."}]}, {"id": "cb5", "stage": "Coursebook", "icon": "💡", "title": "Writing Tips", "fa": "نکات نوشتن", "parts": [{"t": "writingPoints", "title": "Adverbs of attitude", "html": "<h3>قیدهای نگرش (adverbs of attitude)</h3>\n<p>از قیدهایی مثل <b>fortunately, unfortunately, amazingly</b> برای نشان دادن احساس یا نگرش خودتان نسبت به یک اتفاق استفاده کنید.</p>\n<div class=\"ex\">Fortunately, there were some great guides.</div>\n<div class=\"ex\">I didn't see a quetzal bird, unfortunately.</div>\n<div class=\"ex\">Amazingly, it wasn't really scary.</div>\n<div class=\"note\">این قیدها معمولاً در ابتدا یا انتهای جمله می‌آیند و با کاما (,) از بقیه‌ی جمله جدا می‌شوند.</div>"}]}, {"id": "cb6", "stage": "Coursebook", "icon": "✍️", "title": "Write about a trip", "fa": "درباره‌ی یک سفر بنویسید", "parts": [{"t": "writing", "key": "taskOnly"}]}, {"id": "ex1", "stage": "Extra", "icon": "📚", "title": "Vocabulary 1", "fa": "لغات ۱", "parts": [{"t": "vocab", "from": 0, "to": 10}, {"t": "matching", "sets": [1, 2]}]}, {"id": "ex2", "stage": "Extra", "icon": "📚", "title": "Vocabulary 2", "fa": "لغات ۲", "parts": [{"t": "vocab", "from": 10, "to": 20}, {"t": "matching", "sets": [3, 4]}, {"t": "gap"}]}, {"id": "ex3", "stage": "Extra", "icon": "📖", "title": "Article 1", "fa": "مقاله ۱", "parts": [{"t": "reading", "text": 0}]}, {"id": "ex4", "stage": "Extra", "icon": "📖", "title": "Article 2", "fa": "مقاله ۲", "parts": [{"t": "reading", "text": 1}]}, {"id": "ex5", "stage": "Extra", "icon": "✍️", "title": "Writing", "fa": "نوشتن", "parts": [{"t": "writing"}]}];

/* ---- Unit 3 Lesson A: Superlatives ---- */
LESSONS["3A"].title="World Superlatives";
LESSONS["3A"].titleFa="برترین‌های جهان";
LESSONS["3A"].quiz3A=[{"q": "Which city has the tallest office building in the world? (509 meters / 1,670 feet tall)", "o": ["Kuala Lumpur", "Taipei", "Chicago"], "a": 1, "ex": ""}, {"q": "Where is the longest suspension bridge? (1,990 meters / 6,529 feet long)", "o": ["Japan", "Denmark", "China"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "Where is the largest shopping mall? (about 1.97 million square meters)", "o": ["Canada", "China", "The United States"], "a": 1, "ex": ""}, {"q": "Where is the busiest fast-food restaurant in the world? (serves over 40,000 people a day)", "o": ["Seoul", "Moscow", "Hong Kong"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "Which city has the biggest soccer stadium in Europe? (holds nearly 100,000 people)", "o": ["London", "Dublin", "Barcelona"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "Which country has the most tourism? (80 million visitors a year)", "o": ["The United States", "Spain", "France"], "a": 2, "ex": ""}];
LESSONS["3A"].pretest=[{"q": "What's the _____ train station in the world? (big)", "o": ["biggest", "most big"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "What's the _____ airport in the world? (busy)", "o": ["busiest", "most busy"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "Where is the _____ building in the world? (large)", "o": ["largest", "most large"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "What's the _____ city in the world? (expensive)", "o": ["most expensive", "expensivest"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}];
LESSONS["3A"].grammar={points:[{"label": "نقطه ۱", "title": "Short adjectives: the + adjective + -est", "html": "<h3>صفت عالی (Superlative) چیست؟</h3>\n<p>وقتی می‌خواهیم بگوییم چیزی در مقایسه با <b>همه‌ی موارد دیگر</b> در یک گروه، بیشترین یا کمترین ویژگی را دارد، از <b>صفت عالی</b> استفاده می‌کنیم — نه فقط مقایسه‌ی دو چیز با هم (که به آن صفت تفضیلی یا comparative می‌گویند)، بلکه مقایسه با کل یک گروه یا دسته.</p>\n<div class=\"ex\">Tokyo is <span class=\"hl\">the biggest</span> city in Japan. <span class=\"note\">(در مقایسه با همه‌ی شهرهای ژاپن)</span></div>\n<div class=\"note\">صفت عالی همیشه با <b>the</b> می‌آید، چون به یک مورد خاص و یکتا اشاره دارد.</div>\n<h3>قاعده</h3>\n<p>برای صفت‌های کوتاه (معمولاً یک یا دو هجا)، به آخر صفت <b>-est</b> اضافه می‌کنیم.</p>\n<div class=\"ex\">What's the <span class=\"hl\">tallest</span> building in the world?</div>\n<div class=\"ex\">What's the <span class=\"hl\">busiest</span> restaurant?</div>"}, {"label": "نقطه ۲", "title": "Long adjectives: the most/least + adjective", "html": "<h3>قاعده</h3>\n<p>برای صفت‌های بلندتر، از <b>the most</b> یا <b>the least</b> قبل از صفت استفاده می‌کنیم.</p>\n<div class=\"ex\">What's the <span class=\"hl\">most interesting</span> city in your country?</div>\n<div class=\"ex\">What's the <span class=\"hl\">least expensive</span> store?</div>"}, {"label": "نقطه ۳", "title": "Irregular superlatives", "html": "<h3>صفت‌های بی‌قاعده</h3>\n<div class=\"ex\">good → the <span class=\"hl\">best</span> · bad → the <span class=\"hl\">worst</span></div>\n<div class=\"ex\">What's the best country to visit? · What's the worst problem in your country?</div>"}, {"label": "نقطه ۴", "title": "Superlatives with nouns", "html": "<h3>قاعده</h3>\n<p>برای مقایسه با اسم (نه صفت)، از <b>the most + اسم</b> استفاده می‌کنید.</p>\n<div class=\"ex\">Which country has the <span class=\"hl\">most tourism</span>?</div>\n<div class=\"ex\">Which stadium has the <span class=\"hl\">most seats</span>?</div>\n<div class=\"note\">اشتباه رایج: نگویید <s>the most tall building</s> — برای صفت کوتاه tall باید بگویید the tallest.</div>"}],bookExA:[{"q": "What's the _____ (large) city in your country?", "o": ["largest", "most large"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "Which airport has the _____ flights every day?", "o": ["most", "biggest"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "What's the _____ (fast) way to travel?", "o": ["fastest", "most fast"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "What's the _____ (beautiful) region?", "o": ["most beautiful", "beautifulest"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "Which city has the _____ tourism?", "o": ["most", "biggest"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "Where's the _____ (famous) monument?", "o": ["most famous", "famousest"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "What's the _____ (good) university?", "o": ["best", "goodest"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "What's the _____ (bad) problem for people?", "o": ["worst", "baddest"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "Which city has the _____ (big) population?", "o": ["biggest", "most big"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}],extraQuiz1:[{"q": "This is the _____ building in the city. (tall)", "o": ["tallest", "most tall"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "It's the _____ mall in the country. (large)", "o": ["most large", "largest"], "a": 1, "ex": ""}, {"q": "She's the _____ student in the class. (smart)", "o": ["smartest", "most smart"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "This is the _____ interesting museum I've seen. (interesting)", "o": ["most", "-est"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "He's the _____ singer in the group. (good)", "o": ["best", "goodest"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "This is the _____ problem we have. (bad)", "o": ["worst", "baddest"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "Which team has the _____ fans?", "o": ["most", "biggest ones"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "It's the _____ (busy) airport in Asia.", "o": ["busiest", "most busy"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "This is the _____ (expensive) restaurant in town.", "o": ["most expensive", "expensivest"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "That's the _____ (funny) movie I've seen this year.", "o": ["funniest", "most funny"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}],extraQuiz2:[{"q": "She's the _____ (famous) actor in the country.", "o": ["most famous", "famousest"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "This is the _____ (old) building in the city.", "o": ["oldest", "most old"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "He's the _____ (fast) runner on the team.", "o": ["fastest", "most fast"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "That's the _____ (bad) traffic I've seen.", "o": ["worst", "baddest"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "Which country has the _____ population?", "o": ["most", "biggest one"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "This is the _____ (beautiful) beach on the coast.", "o": ["most beautiful", "beautifulest"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "He's the _____ (good) teacher I've ever had.", "o": ["best", "goodest"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "It's the _____ (safe) neighborhood in the city.", "o": ["safest", "most safe"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "This is the _____ (crowded) mall on weekends.", "o": ["most crowded", "crowdedest"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "That's the _____ (dangerous) road in the country.", "o": ["most dangerous", "dangerousest"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}]};
LESSONS["3A"].convo1=[{"q": "What's the most interesting place you've ever visited?", "sample": "Honestly, the most interesting place I've ever been to is probably Istanbul. It's got the most amazing mix of old and new you can imagine — like, some of the oldest buildings in the world are literally right next to the busiest, most modern shopping streets. Walking around, you'll see a centuries-old mosque and then turn a corner into a street full of trendy cafés. The food there is also some of the best I've ever had, honestly. Out of every trip I've taken so far, it's definitely the most memorable one, and I'd go back in a heartbeat if I had the chance.", "glossary": {}, "hl": ["most interesting", "most amazing", "oldest", "busiest", "most memorable"]}];
LESSONS["3A"].convo2=[{"q": "In your opinion, what's the best and the worst thing about your city?", "sample": "I'd say the best thing about my city is definitely the food — we've got some of the most delicious street food you'll find anywhere, and it's ridiculously cheap too. The worst thing, though, is probably the traffic; it's honestly the most stressful part of my whole day, especially in the mornings when everyone's trying to get to work at once. I've thought about moving somewhere quieter more than once, but at the end of the day, it's still the most comfortable place for me to live, mostly because my whole family and all my old friends are here. So even with the traffic, I don't think I'd trade it.", "glossary": {}, "hl": ["best", "most delicious", "worst", "most stressful", "most comfortable"]}];
LESSONS["3A"].sessions=[{"id": "cb1", "stage": "Coursebook", "icon": "❓", "title": "Superlatives Quiz", "fa": "آزمون: برترین‌های جهان", "parts": [{"t": "selfcheck", "key": "quiz3A", "label": "Context quiz"}]}, {"id": "cb2", "stage": "Coursebook", "icon": "⭕", "title": "Pre-test", "fa": "پیش‌آزمون", "parts": [{"t": "selfcheck", "key": "pretest", "label": "Pre-test"}]}, {"id": "cb3", "stage": "Coursebook", "icon": "📝", "title": "Superlatives", "fa": "آموزش: صفت عالی", "parts": [{"t": "teach", "pts": [0, 1, 2, 3]}]}, {"id": "cb4", "stage": "Coursebook", "icon": "✅", "title": "Exercise", "fa": "تمرین A کتاب", "parts": [{"t": "bookExercise", "key": "bookExA", "label": "Exercise"}]}, {"id": "ex1", "stage": "Extra", "icon": "📚", "title": "Vocabulary 1", "fa": "لغات ۱", "parts": [{"t": "vocab", "from": 0, "to": 10}, {"t": "matching", "sets": [1, 2]}]}, {"id": "ex2", "stage": "Extra", "icon": "📚", "title": "Vocabulary 2", "fa": "لغات ۲", "parts": [{"t": "vocab", "from": 10, "to": 20}, {"t": "matching", "sets": [3, 4]}, {"t": "gap"}]}, {"id": "ex3", "stage": "Extra", "icon": "🎯", "title": "Grammar Quiz 1", "fa": "آزمون گرامر ۱", "parts": [{"t": "quizset", "key": "extraQuiz1", "label": "Grammar Quiz 1"}]}, {"id": "ex4", "stage": "Extra", "icon": "🎯", "title": "Grammar Quiz 2", "fa": "آزمون گرامر ۲", "parts": [{"t": "quizset", "key": "extraQuiz2", "label": "Grammar Quiz 2"}]}, {"id": "ex5", "stage": "Extra", "icon": "🗣️", "title": "Conversation Practice 1", "fa": "تمرین مکالمه ۱", "parts": [{"t": "convo", "key": "convo1"}]}, {"id": "ex6", "stage": "Extra", "icon": "🗣️", "title": "Conversation Practice 2", "fa": "تمرین مکالمه ۲", "parts": [{"t": "convo", "key": "convo2"}]}, {"id": "ex7", "stage": "Extra", "icon": "📖", "title": "Article 1", "fa": "مقاله ۱", "parts": [{"t": "reading", "text": 0}]}, {"id": "ex8", "stage": "Extra", "icon": "📖", "title": "Article 2", "fa": "مقاله ۲", "parts": [{"t": "reading", "text": 1}]}, {"id": "ex9", "stage": "Extra", "icon": "✍️", "title": "Writing", "fa": "نوشتن", "parts": [{"t": "writing"}]}];

/* ---- Unit 3 Lesson B: How + adjective ---- */
LESSONS["3B"].title="How Big, How High, How Far?";
LESSONS["3B"].titleFa="چقدر بزرگ، چقدر بلند؟";
LESSONS["3B"].pretest=[{"q": "How _____ is the Nile River?", "o": ["long", "longly"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "It's 6,695 kilometers _____.", "o": ["long", "longly"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "How _____ is Mount Everest?", "o": ["high", "tall only"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "It's 8,850 meters _____.", "o": ["high", "highly"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}];
LESSONS["3B"].grammar={points:[{"label": "نقطه ۱", "title": "Questions with How + adjective ...?", "html": "<h3>قاعده</h3>\n<p>برای پرسیدن اندازه‌ی دقیق چیزی، از <b>How + صفت</b> استفاده می‌کنیم.</p>\n<div class=\"ex\">How high is Mount Everest? → It's 8,850 meters (29,035 feet) high.</div>\n<div class=\"ex\">How long is the Nile River? → It's 6,695 kilometers (4,160 miles) long.</div>\n<div class=\"ex\">How wide is the Grand Canyon? → It's about 29 kilometers (18 miles) wide.</div>\n<div class=\"ex\">How deep is the Pacific Ocean? → It's about 11,000 meters (36,000 feet) deep.</div>\n<div class=\"ex\">How hot does it get in Death Valley? → It can reach 48 degrees Celsius (120 degrees Fahrenheit).</div>"}, {"label": "نقطه ۲", "title": "Measurements + adjective", "html": "<h3>قاعده</h3>\n<p>بعد از یک عدد و واحد اندازه‌گیری، می‌توانیم صفتی مثل <b>high, tall, long, wide, deep</b> اضافه کنیم.</p>\n<div class=\"ex\">It's 8,850 meters <span class=\"hl\">high</span>. · It's 29 kilometers <span class=\"hl\">wide</span>.</div>"}],bookExA:[{"q": "How _____ is the Mackenzie River? — It's 4,241 kilometers long.", "o": ["long", "far"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "How high is Mount Aconcagua? — It's _____ meters high.", "o": ["6,962", "4,241"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "How _____ is Australia? — It's almost 7.7 million square kilometers.", "o": ["large", "tall"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "How wide is the Grand Canyon? — It's _____ kilometers wide.", "o": ["29", "6,962"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "How deep is Lake Baikal? — It's _____ meters deep.", "o": ["1,741", "29"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "How cold does it get in Antarctica? — It can reach _____ degrees Celsius.", "o": ["-89.6", "48"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}],buildingVocab:[{"q": "A large area of sand with very little rain is a...", "o": ["desert", "glacier"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "A group of islands close together is an...", "o": ["archipelago", "reef"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "A large area of trees that gets a lot of rain is a...", "o": ["rain forest", "coast"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "A large body of salt water, bigger than a sea, is an...", "o": ["ocean", "lake"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "A mountain that can erupt is a...", "o": ["volcano", "island"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "A large area of slowly-moving ice is a...", "o": ["glacier", "desert"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "Land completely surrounded by water is an...", "o": ["island", "coast"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "A structure of coral under the sea is a...", "o": ["reef", "river"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "The land next to the sea is the...", "o": ["coast", "mountain"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "A body of fresh water surrounded by land is a...", "o": ["lake", "ocean"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}],extraQuiz1:[{"q": "How _____ is the Amazon River?", "o": ["long", "far"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "It's about 6,400 kilometers _____.", "o": ["long", "longly"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "How _____ is K2? — It's 8,611 meters high.", "o": ["high", "tall only"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "How _____ is the Dead Sea? — It's about 430 meters below sea level.", "o": ["deep", "wide"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "How _____ is the Bering Strait? — It's about 82 kilometers wide.", "o": ["wide", "deep"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "How hot does it get in the Sahara? — It can reach 50 degrees _____.", "o": ["Celsius", "kilometers"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "How _____ is Lake Superior? — It's about 560 kilometers long.", "o": ["long", "high"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "It's 3,000 meters _____ at its deepest point.", "o": ["deep", "wide"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "How _____ is Angel Falls? — It's 979 meters high.", "o": ["high", "long"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "How _____ is the Strait of Gibraltar? — It's about 13 kilometers wide.", "o": ["wide", "deep"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}],extraQuiz2:[{"q": "How _____ is Lake Baikal? — It's 1,642 meters deep.", "o": ["deep", "wide"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "How _____ is the Yangtze River? — It's about 6,300 kilometers long.", "o": ["long", "high"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "How _____ is Denali? — It's 6,190 meters high.", "o": ["high", "deep"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "It's about 1,500 meters _____ at its widest point.", "o": ["wide", "long"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "How _____ does it get in Siberia in winter? — It can reach -50 degrees Celsius.", "o": ["cold", "hot"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "How _____ is the Mariana Trench? — It's about 11,000 meters deep.", "o": ["deep", "high"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "How _____ is the Great Barrier Reef? — It's about 2,300 kilometers long.", "o": ["long", "wide"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "How _____ is Ben Nevis? — It's 1,345 meters high.", "o": ["high", "long"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "It's about 160 kilometers _____ from end to end.", "o": ["long", "deep"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "How _____ is the Colorado River? — It's about 2,300 kilometers long.", "o": ["long", "wide"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}]};
LESSONS["3B"].convo1=[{"q": "What's an amazing natural place you've heard of or visited?", "sample": "I've always wanted to see the Grand Canyon in person — it's incredibly wide, like almost 29 kilometers across at some points, which is honestly hard to even picture. I haven't actually been there yet, but I've seen so many pictures and videos, and it looks absolutely amazing, like nothing else on earth. How deep do you think it actually is? I read somewhere that it's almost 1,800 meters deep in places, which just seems impossible until you see the photos. I'm hoping to finally go next year if everything works out — it's honestly at the top of my travel list right now.", "glossary": {}, "hl": ["wide", "deep", "kilometers", "meters"]}];
LESSONS["3B"].convo2=[{"q": "If you could visit any natural wonder in the world, which would you choose?", "sample": "Probably Mount Everest, if I'm being honest — even just to see it up close from a distance, not to climb it. It's so incredibly high, almost 8,850 meters, that it's genuinely hard to picture until you're standing near it. I definitely wouldn't want to actually climb it, though — that's a whole different level of adventure that I'm just not brave enough for! I'd also love to see the Sahara Desert someday; it's absolutely huge, something like 9 million square kilometers, which is bigger than a lot of entire countries put together. It's honestly hard to imagine how large that really is until you try to compare it to somewhere familiar.", "glossary": {}, "hl": ["high", "meters", "large", "square kilometers"]}];
LESSONS["3B"].sessions=[{"id": "cb1", "stage": "Coursebook", "icon": "💬", "title": "Did You Know...?", "fa": "متن: آیا می‌دانستید؟", "parts": [{"t": "context", "label": "Context", "title": "Did You Know...?", "lines": [{"sp": "Did you know...?", "text": "The Nile is the longest river in Africa. It's 6,695 kilometers (4,160 miles) long."}, {"sp": "Did you know...?", "text": "The highest mountain in the world is Mount Everest in Asia. It's 8,850 meters (29,035 feet) high."}, {"sp": "Did you know...?", "text": "The largest ocean is the Pacific. It covers one-third of the earth! The deepest part is about 11,000 meters (36,000 feet) deep."}, {"sp": "Did you know...?", "text": "The largest river (by area covered) is the Amazon in South America — about 4 million square kilometers (1.5 million square miles)."}, {"sp": "Did you know...?", "text": "The largest hot desert is the Sahara in Africa — about 9.1 million square kilometers (3.5 million square miles)."}, {"sp": "Did you know...?", "text": "The most active volcano is probably Kilauea, on the island of Hawai'i. It has been active since 1983, and it still erupts every day!"}]}]}, {"id": "cb2", "stage": "Coursebook", "icon": "⭕", "title": "Pre-test", "fa": "پیش‌آزمون", "parts": [{"t": "selfcheck", "key": "pretest", "label": "Pre-test"}]}, {"id": "cb3", "stage": "Coursebook", "icon": "📝", "title": "How + Adjective", "fa": "آموزش: How + صفت", "parts": [{"t": "teach", "pts": [0, 1]}]}, {"id": "cb4", "stage": "Coursebook", "icon": "✅", "title": "Exercise", "fa": "تمرین A کتاب", "parts": [{"t": "bookExercise", "key": "bookExA", "label": "Exercise"}]}, {"id": "cb5", "stage": "Coursebook", "icon": "🔁", "title": "Building Vocabulary", "fa": "تقویت واژگان", "parts": [{"t": "bookExercise", "key": "buildingVocab", "label": "Building Vocabulary"}]}, {"id": "ex1", "stage": "Extra", "icon": "📚", "title": "Vocabulary 1", "fa": "لغات ۱", "parts": [{"t": "vocab", "from": 0, "to": 10}, {"t": "matching", "sets": [1, 2]}]}, {"id": "ex2", "stage": "Extra", "icon": "📚", "title": "Vocabulary 2", "fa": "لغات ۲", "parts": [{"t": "vocab", "from": 10, "to": 20}, {"t": "matching", "sets": [3, 4]}, {"t": "gap"}]}, {"id": "ex3", "stage": "Extra", "icon": "🎯", "title": "Grammar Quiz 1", "fa": "آزمون گرامر ۱", "parts": [{"t": "quizset", "key": "extraQuiz1", "label": "Grammar Quiz 1"}]}, {"id": "ex4", "stage": "Extra", "icon": "🎯", "title": "Grammar Quiz 2", "fa": "آزمون گرامر ۲", "parts": [{"t": "quizset", "key": "extraQuiz2", "label": "Grammar Quiz 2"}]}, {"id": "ex5", "stage": "Extra", "icon": "🗣️", "title": "Conversation Practice 1", "fa": "تمرین مکالمه ۱", "parts": [{"t": "convo", "key": "convo1"}]}, {"id": "ex6", "stage": "Extra", "icon": "🗣️", "title": "Conversation Practice 2", "fa": "تمرین مکالمه ۲", "parts": [{"t": "convo", "key": "convo2"}]}, {"id": "ex7", "stage": "Extra", "icon": "📖", "title": "Article 1", "fa": "مقاله ۱", "parts": [{"t": "reading", "text": 0}]}, {"id": "ex8", "stage": "Extra", "icon": "📖", "title": "Article 2", "fa": "مقاله ۲", "parts": [{"t": "reading", "text": 1}]}, {"id": "ex9", "stage": "Extra", "icon": "✍️", "title": "Writing", "fa": "نوشتن", "parts": [{"t": "writing"}]}];

/* ---- Unit 3 Lesson C: conversation strategies ---- */
LESSONS["3C"].grammar={points:[{"label": "استراتژی ۱", "title": "Short supportive responses with really and sure", "html": "<h3>قاعده</h3>\n<p>برای نشان دادن حمایت و همراهی در مکالمه، از پاسخ‌های کوتاه با <b>really</b> یا <b>sure</b> استفاده می‌کنیم.</p>\n<div class=\"ex\">\"This is the most incredible place!\" → \"Yeah, it <span class=\"hl\">really</span> is.\"</div>\n<div class=\"ex\">\"It feels good to be out of the city.\" → \"It <span class=\"hl\">sure</span> does.\"</div>\n<div class=\"note\">فعل کمکی جمله را تکرار می‌کنیم (is→is, does→does) و really/sure را قبل یا بعد از آن می‌آوریم.</div>"},{"label": "استراتژی ۲", "title": "Using superlatives for emphasis", "html": "<h3>قاعده</h3>\n<p>از صفت عالی (superlative) برای تأکید بر احساس یا نظرتان استفاده می‌کنید، نه فقط برای مقایسه‌ی واقعی.</p>\n<div class=\"ex\">\"This is the <span class=\"hl\">most incredible</span> place!\"</div>\n<div class=\"ex\">\"I had the <span class=\"hl\">best</span> time.\"</div>"}],bookExC4:[{"q": "The weather was great last Saturday. → What's the best response?", "o": ["It really was. I spent the whole day outdoors.", "You're right. We really should.", "Yeah, you sure can.", "No, it really doesn't. That's too bad."], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "This city doesn't have many parks. → What's the best response?", "o": ["No, it really doesn't. That's too bad.", "It really was. I spent the whole day outdoors.", "Yeah. It sure is.", "Yeah, you sure can."], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "We should go hiking sometime. → What's the best response?", "o": ["You're right. We really should.", "It really was. I spent the whole day outdoors.", "Yeah, you sure can.", "Yeah. It sure is."], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "The lake here is a great place to go swimming. → What's the best response?", "o": ["Yeah, you sure can.", "No, it really doesn't. That's too bad.", "You're right. We really should.", "It really was. I spent the whole day outdoors."], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "I like being out of the city. You can hear the birds. → What's the best response?", "o": ["Yeah. It sure is.", "No, it really doesn't. That's too bad.", "You're right. We really should.", "Yeah, you sure can."], "a": 0, "ex": ""}],bookExC6:[{"q": "Where's your favorite place to hang out? — I like going to cafés. You see _____ people. (interesting)", "o": ["the most interesting", "interestinger"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "Where's a good place to get out of the city? — The mountains. It's so quiet, and you can see _____ wildlife. (amazing)", "o": ["the most amazing", "amazingest"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "I heard you can take a boat trip down the river. — You sure can. You can get _____ views of the city. (good)", "o": ["the best", "the goodest"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "How was your vacation? — We went sailing around some islands. I had _____ time. (good)", "o": ["the best", "the goodest"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}]};
LESSONS["3C"].sessions=[{"id": "cs1", "stage": "Coursebook", "icon": "💬", "title": "Conversation", "fa": "متن کامل مکالمه", "parts": [{"t": "context", "label": "Context", "title": "Kim and Diego visit a national park", "lines": [{"sp": "Kim", "text": "This is the most incredible place!"}, {"sp": "Diego", "text": "Yeah, it really is. It feels good to be out of the city."}, {"sp": "Kim", "text": "It sure does. You know, these trees are just awesome."}, {"sp": "Diego", "text": "They really are. Have you ever been to Sequoia National Park?"}, {"sp": "Kim", "text": "No. Have you?"}, {"sp": "Diego", "text": "Yeah. I went last year. The trees there are the tallest in the world."}, {"sp": "Kim", "text": "Really? I didn't know that."}, {"sp": "Diego", "text": "Yeah. I had the best time. I mean, it's just the greatest place to hike."}, {"sp": "Kim", "text": "We should go hiking there sometime."}, {"sp": "Diego", "text": "You're right. We really should."}]}]}, {"id": "cs2", "stage": "Coursebook", "icon": "📝", "title": "Short Responses", "fa": "توضیح: پاسخ‌های کوتاه حمایتی", "parts": [{"t": "teach", "pts": [0]}]}, {"id": "cs3", "stage": "Coursebook", "icon": "👆", "title": "Find the pattern", "fa": "الگو را پیدا کنید", "parts": [{"t": "tapfind", "prompt": "Tap every line where Kim or Diego use a short response with really or sure.", "lines": [{"sp": "Kim", "text": "This is the most incredible place!"}, {"sp": "Diego", "text": "Yeah, it really is. It feels good to be out of the city."}, {"sp": "Kim", "text": "It sure does. You know, these trees are just awesome."}, {"sp": "Diego", "text": "They really are. Have you ever been to Sequoia National Park?"}, {"sp": "Kim", "text": "No. Have you?"}, {"sp": "Diego", "text": "Yeah. I went last year. The trees there are the tallest in the world."}, {"sp": "Kim", "text": "Really? I didn't know that."}, {"sp": "Diego", "text": "Yeah. I had the best time. I mean, it's just the greatest place to hike."}, {"sp": "Kim", "text": "We should go hiking there sometime."}, {"sp": "Diego", "text": "You're right. We really should."}]}]}, {"id": "cs4", "stage": "Coursebook", "icon": "✅", "title": "Exercise", "fa": "تمرین D کتاب", "parts": [{"t": "bookExercise", "key": "bookExC4", "label": "Exercise"}]}, {"id": "cs5", "stage": "Coursebook", "icon": "➕", "title": "Emphasis", "fa": "توضیح: صفت عالی برای تأکید", "parts": [{"t": "teach", "pts": [1]}]}, {"id": "cs6", "stage": "Coursebook", "icon": "✅", "title": "More Practice", "fa": "تمرین صفت عالی", "parts": [{"t": "bookExercise", "key": "bookExC6", "label": "Exercise"}]}, {"id": "ex1", "stage": "Extra", "icon": "📚", "title": "Vocabulary 1", "fa": "لغات ۱", "parts": [{"t": "vocab", "from": 0, "to": 10}, {"t": "matching", "sets": [1, 2]}]}, {"id": "ex2", "stage": "Extra", "icon": "📚", "title": "Vocabulary 2", "fa": "لغات ۲", "parts": [{"t": "vocab", "from": 10, "to": 20}, {"t": "matching", "sets": [3, 4]}, {"t": "gap"}]}, {"id": "ex3", "stage": "Extra", "icon": "📖", "title": "Article 1", "fa": "مقاله ۱", "parts": [{"t": "reading", "text": 0}]}, {"id": "ex4", "stage": "Extra", "icon": "📖", "title": "Article 2", "fa": "مقاله ۲", "parts": [{"t": "reading", "text": 1}]}, {"id": "ex5", "stage": "Extra", "icon": "✍️", "title": "Writing", "fa": "نوشتن", "parts": [{"t": "writing"}]}];

/* ---- Unit 3 Lesson D: reading + writing ---- */
LESSONS["3D"].mainReading=[{"title": "World Records", "topic": "Popular videos, longest, most dangerous, oldest", "text": "WHAT WAS MORE POPULAR?\nA family video uploaded online showing a baby biting his older brother's finger, or a popular video war game?\n\n\"Charlie bit my finger\" made the record books as the most liked video in one year with 908,668 \"likes.\" The video war game, however, sold 6.5 million copies in the first 24 hours of its launch in the United States and UK alone.\n\nWHAT'S THE LONGEST?\nThe longest snake in the world, the shortest street, or the world record for the long jump?\n\nThe world's longest snake, a python, is 7.67 meters (25 feet 2 inches) long. It's the scariest inhabitant at a haunted house attraction in Kansas City, Missouri.\n\nMeanwhile, the shortest street in the world, in Caithness, Scotland, is only 2 meters (6 feet 9 inches) long. It consists of one house with the address 1, Ebenezer Place.\n\nThe world record for the long jump was set in 1991. Mike Powell from the United States jumped 8.95 meters (29 feet 4.36 inches) in Tokyo, Japan. More than two decades later, it was still the world record.\n\nWHICH IS MORE DANGEROUS?\nThe most dangerous road in the world, or the most dangerous animal?\n\nThe most dangerous road in the world runs 69 kilometers (43 miles) from La Paz to Coroico in Bolivia. On average there are 300 deaths annually. The road is most dangerous in the rainy season when it is muddy and wet.\n\nThe deadliest animal is the mosquito. This tiny insect can carry a deadly disease, malaria. Malaria kills more than two million people a year.\n\nWHICH IS OLDER?\nThe oldest skyscraper city, or the oldest living tree?\n\nThe oldest skyscraper city in the world is in Yemen. Shibam, with approximately 7,000 citizens, has buildings up to 12 stories high. While they are not the tallest skyscrapers in the world (the tallest is currently in Dubai, UAE), they are the oldest. Most of the 500 skyscrapers were built in the sixteenth century. However, Hong Kong, the place with the most skyscrapers, has 2,354 towering buildings, which together would almost reach a space station orbiting Earth.\n\nSome of the oldest forests in the world are in the Andes, a mountain range in southern Chile and Argentina. The average age of these forests is 2,500 years old. However, the oldest living tree, a pine tree in the White Mountains of California, is 4,800 years old.", "glossary": {}, "hl": ["launch", "inhabitant", "consists of", "annually", "citizens", "towering"], "gist": {"q": "What is this article mainly about?", "o": ["A set of surprising world records on different topics", "A guide to the best places to visit in the world", "The history of video games"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, "detailed": [{"q": "Did the most popular video war game sell 6.5 million copies in one day or one month?", "o": ["One day (in the first 24 hours)", "One month"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "Is the longest snake shorter or longer than the world's longest long jump?", "o": ["Shorter than the long jump record (7.67 m vs. 8.95 m)", "Longer than the long jump record"], "a": 0, "ex": "مار ۷.۶۷ متر است و رکورد پرش طول ۸.۹۵ متر — پس مار کوتاه‌تر است."}, {"q": "Do the people at 1, Ebenezer Place have any next-door neighbors?", "o": ["No — it's the only house on the street", "Yes, several neighbors"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "When is the worst time for accidents on the dangerous road in Bolivia?", "o": ["During the wet, rainy season", "During the cold season"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "Which city has the most skyscrapers — Shibam, Dubai, or Hong Kong?", "o": ["Hong Kong", "Shibam", "Dubai"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "Is the oldest living tree located in one of the oldest forests (the Andes)?", "o": ["No — it's in the White Mountains of California, a different place", "Yes, it's in the Andes"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}]}];
LESSONS["3D"].writingTask={"title": "An interesting place in your country", "text": "Write a short article (100–150 words) about an interesting place in your country — a mountain, a building, a natural feature, or a record-holder of some kind. Use at least one superlative, and add extra information using the apposition pattern from the Help note (Noun, extra info, ...)."};
LESSONS["3D"].grammar={vocabInContext:[{"q": "After a launch, a company starts to _____ a product.", "o": ["sell", "design"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "An inhabitant is a thing or person that _____ a place.", "o": ["lives in", "visits"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "If a street consists of one house, it means it _____ one house.", "o": ["has", "is famous for"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "When something happens annually, it happens every _____.", "o": ["year", "month"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "A city that has 7,000 citizens has 7,000 _____.", "o": ["people", "buildings"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}, {"q": "A towering building is very _____.", "o": ["tall", "short"], "a": 0, "ex": ""}]};
LESSONS["3D"].sessions=[{"id": "cb1", "stage": "Coursebook", "icon": "🔎", "title": "Scan first", "fa": "ابتدا مرور سریع کنید", "parts": [{"t": "scanpre", "src": "mainReading", "text": 0}]}, {"id": "cb2", "stage": "Coursebook", "icon": "📖", "title": "Reading", "fa": "متن کامل", "parts": [{"t": "fullread", "src": "mainReading", "text": 0}]}, {"id": "cb3", "stage": "Coursebook", "icon": "✅", "title": "Comprehension", "fa": "درک مطلب", "parts": [{"t": "comprehension", "src": "mainReading", "text": 0}]}, {"id": "cb4", "stage": "Coursebook", "icon": "🔤", "title": "Vocabulary in context", "fa": "واژگان در متن", "parts": [{"t": "bookExercise", "key": "vocabInContext", "label": "Vocabulary in context"}]}, {"id": "cb5", "stage": "Coursebook", "icon": "📝", "title": "Sample", "fa": "نمونه‌ی نوشتاری", "parts": [{"t": "writingSample", "title": "Mount Aconcagua", "text": "MOUNT ACONCAGUA — THE HIGHEST MOUNTAIN IN ARGENTINA\n\nMount Aconcagua, a peak in the Andes range, is the highest mountain in Argentina. At 6,962 meters (22,841 feet), it is the highest mountain in North and South America. Many people come to Argentina every year to climb Mount Aconcagua and to see the Andes, the longest mountain range in the world."}]}, {"id": "cb6", "stage": "Coursebook", "icon": "💡", "title": "Writing Tips", "fa": "نکات نوشتن", "parts": [{"t": "writingPoints", "title": "Adding information", "html": "<h3>اضافه کردن اطلاعات (Apposition)</h3>\n<p>می‌توانید با قرار دادن یک عبارت توصیفی بلافاصله بعد از اسم (بین دو کاما)، اطلاعات بیشتری به جمله اضافه کنید — بدون نوشتن یک جمله‌ی جداگانه.</p>\n<div class=\"ex\">Mount Aconcagua is the highest mountain in Argentina. + It is a peak in the Andes range. → <b>Mount Aconcagua, a peak in the Andes range, is the highest mountain in Argentina.</b></div>\n<div class=\"ex\">Many people come to see the Andes. + They are the longest mountain range in the world. → <b>Many people come to see the Andes, the longest mountain range in the world.</b></div>"}]}, {"id": "cb7", "stage": "Coursebook", "icon": "✍️", "title": "Write about an interesting place", "fa": "درباره‌ی یک مکان جالب بنویسید", "parts": [{"t": "writing", "key": "taskOnly"}]}, {"id": "ex1", "stage": "Extra", "icon": "📚", "title": "Vocabulary 1", "fa": "لغات ۱", "parts": [{"t": "vocab", "from": 0, "to": 10}, {"t": "matching", "sets": [1, 2]}]}, {"id": "ex2", "stage": "Extra", "icon": "📚", "title": "Vocabulary 2", "fa": "لغات ۲", "parts": [{"t": "vocab", "from": 10, "to": 20}, {"t": "matching", "sets": [3, 4]}, {"t": "gap"}]}, {"id": "ex3", "stage": "Extra", "icon": "📖", "title": "Article 1", "fa": "مقاله ۱", "parts": [{"t": "reading", "text": 0}]}, {"id": "ex4", "stage": "Extra", "icon": "📖", "title": "Article 2", "fa": "مقاله ۲", "parts": [{"t": "reading", "text": 1}]}, {"id": "ex5", "stage": "Extra", "icon": "✍️", "title": "Writing", "fa": "نوشتن", "parts": [{"t": "writing"}]}];
